1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,549
Aarav's bus has a flat fare.

2
00:00:02,549 --> 00:00:07,015
Ride one stop or ten stops, the
ticket costs exactly the same.

3
00:00:07,415 --> 00:00:09,278
At home, the mirror copies him.

4
00:00:09,278 --> 00:00:11,991
Whatever he shows it, the
same thing comes back.

5
00:00:12,391 --> 00:00:15,003
And his uncle has a square plot of land.

6
00:00:15,003 --> 00:00:18,570
Double the side, and the area
becomes four times as big.

7
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:22,754
A fare that never changes, a
perfect copy, and a square.

8
00:00:22,754 --> 00:00:25,055
Three rules that look nothing alike.

9
00:00:25,555 --> 00:00:30,472
In maths, they are the constant function,
the identity function and a polynomial

10
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:31,372
function.

11
00:00:31,215 --> 00:00:32,925
Today we draw all three.

12
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,598
First, the constant function.

13
00:00:35,598 --> 00:00:39,138
f of x equals c, where c
is one fixed real number.

14
00:00:39,538 --> 00:00:41,731
Every input gives the same output.

15
00:00:41,731 --> 00:00:45,356
Put in two, minus five or
a hundred, and out comes c.

16
00:00:45,756 --> 00:00:50,056
So the domain is all of R, but
the range has just one element: c.

17
00:00:50,706 --> 00:00:54,019
Its graph is a flat line,
parallel to the x axis.

18
00:00:54,019 --> 00:00:57,179
Change c, and the whole
line slides up or down.

19
00:00:57,579 --> 00:00:59,594
Next, the identity function.

20
00:00:59,594 --> 00:01:00,961
f of x equals x.

21
00:01:00,961 --> 00:01:04,646
Every input comes back
unchanged, just like the mirror.

22
00:01:05,046 --> 00:01:08,034
Its domain is R, and its range is R too.

23
00:01:08,434 --> 00:01:11,428
Its graph is a straight
line through the origin.

24
00:01:11,428 --> 00:01:13,362
Watch a point slide along it.

25
00:01:13,362 --> 00:01:15,117
x is two, so y is two.

26
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:17,736
x is minus three, so y is minus three.

27
00:01:18,386 --> 00:01:19,507
Side by side.

28
00:01:19,507 --> 00:01:22,216
The constant function ignores the input.

29
00:01:22,216 --> 00:01:23,607
Its line is flat.

30
00:01:24,007 --> 00:01:26,657
The identity function copies the input.

31
00:01:26,657 --> 00:01:30,124
Its line climbs one step
up for every step across.

32
00:01:30,724 --> 00:01:31,838
Now you try.

33
00:01:31,838 --> 00:01:34,920
What is the range of f of x equals five?

34
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,304
Pause and decide.

35
00:01:39,504 --> 00:01:41,549
Just the set with five in it!

36
00:01:41,549 --> 00:01:45,022
Every input gives five, so
the range has one element.

37
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:46,122
Not all of R.

38
00:01:46,772 --> 00:01:47,935
Remember this.

39
00:01:47,935 --> 00:01:50,162
A constant function ignores x.

40
00:01:50,162 --> 00:01:52,444
The identity function copies x.

41
00:01:53,144 --> 00:01:54,970
Now, polynomial functions.

42
00:01:54,970 --> 00:01:59,992
f of x equals a nought, plus a one
x, plus a two x squared, and so on,

43
00:01:59,992 --> 00:02:01,919
up to a n, x to the n.

44
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,929
The a's are real numbers.

45
00:02:03,929 --> 00:02:08,291
And n must be a whole number:
zero, one, two, three, and so on.

46
00:02:09,041 --> 00:02:10,695
The square plot is one.

47
00:02:10,695 --> 00:02:12,300
Its area is s squared.

48
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:15,102
Double the side, and two squared is four.

49
00:02:15,102 --> 00:02:16,552
Four times the area.

50
00:02:17,202 --> 00:02:18,981
Watch what the power does.

51
00:02:18,981 --> 00:02:22,174
Plot y equals x to the
n, and let n count up.

52
00:02:22,574 --> 00:02:23,484
n is zero.

53
00:02:23,484 --> 00:02:26,685
x to the zero is one,
so we get a flat line.

54
00:02:26,685 --> 00:02:28,085
A constant function.

55
00:02:28,485 --> 00:02:29,446
n is one.

56
00:02:29,446 --> 00:02:30,515
y equals x.

57
00:02:30,515 --> 00:02:32,185
The identity function.

58
00:02:32,585 --> 00:02:33,485
n is two.

59
00:02:33,454 --> 00:02:35,687
AU shaped curve, the parabola.

60
00:02:36,087 --> 00:02:37,014
n is three.

61
00:02:37,014 --> 00:02:40,431
The curve falls on the left,
and rises on the right.

62
00:02:41,081 --> 00:02:44,416
So the constant and the
identity are not strangers.

63
00:02:44,416 --> 00:02:47,641
They are the simplest
polynomial functions of all.

64
00:02:48,291 --> 00:02:50,822
But not every formula is a polynomial.

65
00:02:50,822 --> 00:02:53,569
Every power of x must be a whole number.

66
00:02:53,969 --> 00:02:54,869
Quick one.

67
00:02:54,854 --> 00:02:59,360
Is x to the power two thirds,
plus two x, a polynomial function?

68
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,611
Pause and think.

69
00:03:03,811 --> 00:03:04,711
No!

70
00:03:04,272 --> 00:03:08,037
The power two thirds is a
fraction, not a whole number.

71
00:03:08,037 --> 00:03:10,461
So it is not a polynomial function.

72
00:03:11,111 --> 00:03:12,846
Now, one worked example.

73
00:03:13,196 --> 00:03:17,047
f of x equals x cubed,
minus x squared, plus two.

74
00:03:17,047 --> 00:03:18,605
Is it a polynomial?

75
00:03:18,605 --> 00:03:22,304
Find f of minus one, f
of zero, and f of two.

76
00:03:22,804 --> 00:03:23,704
Step one.

77
00:03:23,617 --> 00:03:26,113
The powers are three, two and zero.

78
00:03:26,113 --> 00:03:29,373
All whole numbers, so
yes, it is a polynomial.

79
00:03:30,123 --> 00:03:31,023
Step two.

80
00:03:30,952 --> 00:03:34,550
f of minus one is minus
one, minus one, plus two.

81
00:03:34,550 --> 00:03:35,642
That is zero.

82
00:03:36,392 --> 00:03:37,292
Step three.

83
00:03:37,265 --> 00:03:38,888
f of zero is just two.

84
00:03:39,638 --> 00:03:40,538
Step four.

85
00:03:40,432 --> 00:03:43,160
f of two is eight, minus four, plus two.

86
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,100
That is six.

87
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:49,309
So the graph passes through minus
one, zero, then zero, two, then two,

88
00:03:49,309 --> 00:03:50,209
six.

89
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:51,896
Now, the exam trap.

90
00:03:52,246 --> 00:03:56,283
What is the degree of x plus one,
whole squared, minus x squared?

91
00:03:56,283 --> 00:03:58,969
Many students see the
squares, and say two.

92
00:03:59,369 --> 00:04:00,714
But expand first.

93
00:04:00,714 --> 00:04:05,809
x squared plus two x plus one, minus
x squared, leaves two x plus one.

94
00:04:05,809 --> 00:04:07,270
The degree is one.

95
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:09,581
Always simplify before you judge.

96
00:04:10,231 --> 00:04:11,746
Where is this asked?

97
00:04:11,746 --> 00:04:16,677
We found no past paper question on
just this idea, so no exam lights up.

98
00:04:16,677 --> 00:04:21,069
But these three are the building
blocks of harder function questions in

99
00:04:21,069 --> 00:04:21,969
JEE.

100
00:04:22,187 --> 00:04:23,520
Exam level now.

101
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:25,667
f is a polynomial function.

102
00:04:25,667 --> 00:04:27,011
Find f of two.

103
00:04:27,011 --> 00:04:28,401
Pause and solve.

104
00:04:33,801 --> 00:04:35,039
The answer is C.

105
00:04:35,039 --> 00:04:35,939
Nine.

106
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:37,627
Put x equals zero.

107
00:04:37,627 --> 00:04:40,406
f of one minus f of zero is three.

108
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:42,202
So f of one is four.

109
00:04:42,702 --> 00:04:44,073
Put x equals one.

110
00:04:44,073 --> 00:04:46,517
f of two minus f of one is five.

111
00:04:47,017 --> 00:04:49,485
So f of two is four plus five.

112
00:04:49,485 --> 00:04:50,385
Nine.

113
00:04:50,104 --> 00:04:53,823
In fact, f of x is x
plus one, whole squared.

114
00:04:54,423 --> 00:04:55,887
Here is your recap.

115
00:04:55,887 --> 00:04:57,392
Screenshot this card.

116
00:05:00,592 --> 00:05:03,590
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

117
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:04,890
One.

118
00:05:04,526 --> 00:05:08,600
What is the range of a constant
function f of x equals c?

119
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:10,400
Two.

120
00:05:10,121 --> 00:05:13,129
Is one over x a polynomial function?

121
00:05:13,129 --> 00:05:14,029
Why?

122
00:05:14,651 --> 00:05:15,551
Three.

123
00:05:15,345 --> 00:05:20,704
Find f of three, for f of x equals
x cubed minus x squared plus two.

124
00:05:21,804 --> 00:05:26,951
Next time: distance from home is never
negative, whichever way Aarav rides.

125
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:29,682
Meet the rational and modulus functions.
